{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in one deterministic specification with small helper states. The policy keeps random_walk as the default clear-state action, uses a short forward pulse only from a dedicated progress state, routes every obstacle event through recovery, prefers directed turns for side obstacles, uses brief backward escape for front obstacles, and reserves full_rotate for a last-resort blocked state. Action states self-loop on non-critical path_clear so open-loop pulses are not preempted, while obstacle events still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate environment sensing from motion capability in G so E can impose the policy cleanly.",
    "Use exactly one controllable action per explore/recovery state, with fast return to exploration when path_clear is observed after recovery."
  ],
